1
00:00:00,760 --> 00:00:05,740
Touchline helps football fans and commentators follow a match with statistics and AI explanations.

2
00:00:06,693 --> 00:00:09,227
Open this Azure address to try it yourself.

3
00:00:09,237 --> 00:00:10,765
No installation is needed.

4
00:00:10,775 --> 00:00:14,493
The pitch shows recorded actions in place of broadcast footage.

5
00:00:15,338 --> 00:00:21,140
We use event data: individual passes, shots, and other actions, each with a time, player, and location.

6
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:26,726
This historical Chelsea against Arsenal match simulates live play by streaming one event at a time.

7
00:00:26,736 --> 00:00:29,548
Charts and AI use only the events revealed so far.

8
00:00:30,372 --> 00:00:33,198
At fifteen times speed, match evidence builds quickly.

9
00:00:33,208 --> 00:00:36,822
Watch the clock, statistics, and charts update as each event arrives.

10
00:00:37,643 --> 00:00:39,774
Select a shot to inspect the chance.

11
00:00:39,784 --> 00:00:44,772
The momentum chart compares recent attacking threat, using an expected threat proxy.

12
00:00:44,782 --> 00:00:46,795
Its timeline grows with the match.

13
00:00:46,805 --> 00:00:49,413
Passing networks show which players connect.

14
00:00:51,162 --> 00:00:54,115
Narration adds short, timestamped match notes automatically.

15
00:00:54,125 --> 00:00:58,312
It follows the evidence as play develops, so you can watch without typing a question.

16
00:01:01,069 --> 00:01:05,905
Switch to Ask the match for a specific question: who has created the better chances?

17
00:01:05,915 --> 00:01:08,154
Answers use the current match snapshot.

18
00:01:08,164 --> 00:01:11,039
Switching modes keeps your notes and conversation.

19
00:01:13,718 --> 00:01:16,357
Historical events enter FastAPI one at a time.

20
00:01:16,367 --> 00:01:20,042
Its analytics update browser charts through a live event stream.

21
00:01:20,052 --> 00:01:27,354
For narration and questions, Microsoft Agent Framework runs three tools: match statistics, recent events, and player summaries.

22
00:01:27,364 --> 00:01:30,406
Azure GPT four point one mini explains that evidence.

23
00:01:30,416 --> 00:01:35,588
The server checks the answer format and event references before sending it to the browser.

24
00:01:41,061 --> 00:01:47,230
Try the live app: choose a fixture, start a replay, and explore both AI modes.

25
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:49,289
Developed by Hadi Sotudeh.

26
00:01:49,299 --> 00:01:51,824
For more, follow me on LinkedIn.

27
00:01:51,834 --> 00:01:52,141
Bye.
